menu "zlib Configurations"

    config ZLIB_PREFER_PSRAM
        bool "Prefer PSRAM for zlib's own allocations"
        depends on SPIRAM
        default y
        help
            Route the memory zlib allocates for itself through heap_caps, so
            its large working buffers can live in PSRAM. Internal 8-bit RAM is
            used as a fallback when PSRAM is not initialized or cannot satisfy
            an allocation. Requests below 16 KiB keep preferring internal RAM.

            Without this option zlib calls malloc(). With
            CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_CAPS_ALLOC, malloc() never returns PSRAM; with
            CONFIG_SPIRAM_USE_MALLOC, only requests above
            CONFIG_SPIRAM_MALLOC_ALWAYSINTERNAL do. Enabling this option is
            therefore the only way to move zlib's working buffers out of
            internal RAM in either configuration.

            The component's zcalloc()/zcfree() are compiled in either way; this
            option only selects which allocator they call.

            Only the allocator zlib uses for its own state and buffers is
            affected. The compression and decompression buffers an application
            passes in are its own, and are allocated by the application.

            A custom allocator installed in z_stream.zalloc/zfree always wins
            over this option, as zlib documents.

            PSRAM is slower than internal RAM, so compression and
            decompression run slower with this option enabled.

endmenu
